Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 19 03:05:35 2026 +0000

    program layer: an item's law families are judged once, on its view, under its one law_findings

    The seventeen per-item fact queries the laws read (misses, receivers, copies, breaches, ungiven, unmet,
    unknown types, misnamed, coalesces, externs, generic methods, instance checks, methods taken, unwritten,
    seats, unreached, registry holes) are no queries: each is made the first time a law of it asks, held on
    the item's view, and read by its other laws. law_findings holds its item's view while its laws run, so
    judging one item reads other items without its view passing. item_refusals stays a query. The four
    file-level checks a build's refusal reads ask whether the file's findings hold a law of the family.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
